music BGM08D.mp3
text Saturday morning.
text I'm standing in front of Furukawa's parents' by myself.
text How shocked are they going to be to learn that a man's taking their daughter away from them?
text I don't have any way of knowing.
text But then I think about how I would feel if someone else stole Nagisa away from me. I realize it would feel as though I'd been thrown into a pit of despair.
text If my actions are going to make them suffer that much, then...
text No. I still want Nagisa even if it means doing that.
text If there's one thing I can say about myself, it's that no one in the world needs Nagisa more than I do.
text And I believe that Nagisa thinks the same.
text So it doesn't matter who tries to get in our way.
text I'm going to face this like a man.
text I begin walking again.
